# Trivy ignore list — reviewed, non-applicable advisories only.
# Mirrors the accepted-risk set in osv-scanner.toml and pnpm.auditConfig
# (package.json). Keep the rationale in sync across all three.

# react-router RSC-mode CSRF bypass. The client is a Vite SPA using
# react-router in library mode only (no RSC), so it does not apply. The fix
# (react-router 8) requires a React 18->19 migration, tracked separately.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# brace-expansion ReDoS. The tree resolves to 1.1.16/2.1.2/5.0.8, all at or
# above the maintainer's per-line security patches (1.1.12/2.0.2/5.0.8); OSV's
# affected-versions list for the 1.x line tops out at 1.1.11, so 1.1.16 is
# patched. The scanners over-report across major lines. CVE-2026-14257 is the
# CVE alias of GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (Trivy matches by CVE); both are listed.
GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg
CVE-2026-14257

# image-size infinite-loop DoS (crafted JXL/HEIF box-types, and a zero-length
# ICNS entry). No fixed version exists — OSV lists every version through 2.0.2
# as affected, including the whole 2.x line — so there is nothing to bump to.
# Reached only via metro -> @react-native/community-cli-plugin, React Native's
# build-time bundler; the images parsed are this repo's committed assets, not
# remote input. Mirrored in osv-scanner.toml with an ignoreUntil of 2026-11-30.
# CVE aliases listed alongside the GHSAs because Trivy matches by CVE.
GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq
CVE-2025-71329
GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr
CVE-2025-71330

# Twisted 26.4.0 (apps/blackout-server/poetry.lock): three HIGH denial-of-service
# advisories whose only fix is the 26.10.0rc1 pre-release (2026-10-22), which is
# not locked. Each is in a protocol implementation Synapse never imports:
# twisted.words.xish (XMPP XML stream), twisted.words.protocols.irc, and
# twisted.conch.telnet; the manhole uses twisted.conch.manhole_ssh, not telnet.
# Remove these three entries when Twisted 26.10.0 final is locked. CVE aliases
# listed because Trivy matches by CVE. Record:
# docs/security/synapse-dependencies-triage-2026-10-25.md. Review by 2026-12-31.
GHSA-3476-c5c2-fr73
CVE-2026-115775
GHSA-53xc-49m8-p798
CVE-2026-115776
GHSA-cwm5-jh59-mwxr
CVE-2026-115778

# Twisted 26.4.0: HTTP/2 "rapid reset" CPU exhaustion in twisted.web._http2
# (published 2026-10-29, no CVE). Fixed in 26.10.0rc1; 26.10.0 final was
# published on 2026-10-30 and is not locked yet. No Blackout listener can speak
# HTTP/2: Twisted switches to H2Connection only when TLS ALPN negotiates "h2"
# and the h2 and priority packages import, and neither package is in
# poetry.lock or the image (twisted.web.http.H2_ENABLED is False there).
# Synapse's TLS context sets no ALPN, every shipped listener is tls: false, and
# nginx reaches Synapse with proxy_pass http:// (Twisted has no cleartext
# HTTP/2). Remove this entry,
# with the three above, when Twisted 26.10.0 is locked; it expires on
# 2026-11-30 so the gate fails again if that has not happened. Record:
# docs/security/dependency-advisories-server-desktop-2026-10-30.md.
GHSA-vpp8-g58w-m8mp exp:2026-11-30
